# Docker build context for this workspace is the REPOSITORY ROOT (not
# servers/management/), because servers/management/Dockerfile needs the
# workspace-root uv.lock (see that file's own top-of-file comment for why).
# Docker resolves `.dockerignore` relative to the build context root, so
# this file lives here rather than next to the Dockerfile.

# Secrets — never let a stray local .env reach the image (AC-007-4).
# `.env.*` (not just `.env`) so a rotation/backup file (e.g. `.env.bak.*`)
# never enters the build context either — .gitignore already ignores these
# for git; this file must match it 1:1, since `COPY . /app` in the builder
# stage would otherwise still pull a live secret into a build cache layer
# (security review finding, 2026-09-16).
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*

# Local virtual environments — rebuilt inside the image by `uv sync`, and
# copying a host-built one in (macOS arm64 Mach-O binaries, wrong Python
# ABI) would corrupt the Linux venv the Dockerfile itself builds.
.venv/
**/.venv/

# Version control / workspace tooling docs — not part of the runtime
# artifact, and .claude/ in particular is this repo's FRD/PLAN workflow
# scratch space, not application config.
.git/
.claude/

# Python bytecode / cache
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Test suite — not needed at runtime; TASK-031's CI runs tests from source
# (via `uv run pytest`) before the image build, not from inside the image.
**/tests/

# Lint / type-check / test caches
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.pyright/
**/.pyright/

# Build artifacts (matches .gitignore) — irrelevant to `uv sync`, which
# rebuilds the wheel it needs from source inside the image.
dist/
**/dist/
build/
**/build/
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
